  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Work has already been submitted for this by ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "accessLevel": "",
        "id": "557058:d68ad01c-c97b-42a0-8679-bae8450078ab",
        "localId": "78325a6f-6ff7-4334-bda4-7ffdef91784e",
        "text": "@James Alexander"
       },
       "type": "mention"
      },
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "PR to follow shortly",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "em"
        }
       ],
       "text": "I have bumped the versions of Amazon Linux and Postgres SQL to that the script will deploy without giving errors. I have moved the versions of software into ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://variables.tf"
         },
         "type": "link"
        },
        {
         "type": "em"
        }
       ],
       "text": "variables.tf",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "em"
        }
       ],
       "text": " so that editing ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://main.tf"
         },
         "type": "link"
        },
        {
         "type": "em"
        }
       ],
       "text": "main.tf",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "em"
        }
       ],
       "text": "  should usually be unnecessary when updating versions in future.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "em"
        }
       ],
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "em"
        }
       ],
       "text": "I have reduced the number of variables one needs to supply: a user now needs to supply only the bucket name. Terraform will pick up default profile values (if the user has an AWS profile). Supplying the EC2 keypair is also optional - it always was - but the documentation isn’t clear on this.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
